| one persistent program, no per-kernel completion | Groq/Cerebras static scheduling; GPU megakernels | software or silicon | A1→A2 +{{ ((K.abl_by.A2.tok_s_user/K.abl_by.A1.tok_s_user-1)*100)|n(0) }}% (barriers), A2→A3 +{{ ((K.abl_by.A3.tok_s_user/K.abl_by.A2.tok_s_user-1)*100)|n(0) }}% (flags) |
| Belady/MIN-optimal weight prefetch | caching theory: the static schedule *is* the future reference string | software (TMA L2 prefetch) or silicon (staging SRAM) | A3→A4 +{{ ((K.abl_by.A4.tok_s_user/K.abl_by.A3.tok_s_user-1)*100)|n(0) }}% |
| in-network all-reduce | HPC (BlueGene, Anton) | already in the GPU baseline (NVLS reduces in the switch); MDA-1 assumes no faster link | ±0 by construction |
| on-chip hand-off, HW router, Engram off-HBM | Etched-style specialization | silicon only | A4→A5 {{ sp(K.abl_by.A5.tok_s_user/K.abl_by.A4.tok_s_user - 1) }} at 4 chips |
| LRU/LFU cache of experts | CDN / CPU caches | SRAM expert cache | **no**: half of MDA-1's SRAM holds {{ D.expert_cache.slots_per_layer_in_half_sram|n(1) }} expert slices per layer; a {{ D.expert_cache.curves.lru[3].hit|pct }} LRU hit needs {{ D.expert_cache.curves.lru[3].sram_gb_per_chip|n(0) }} GB per chip |
